<|im_start|>user
Problem: The sequences $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ and $\left\{b_{n}\right\}$ are arithmetic sequences with the sums of their first $n$ terms being $S_{n}$ and $T_{n}$, respectively. Given that $\frac{S_{n}}{T_{n}}=\frac{2 n}{3 n+1}$, determine $\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{a_{n}}{b_{n}}$.

A. 1

B. $\frac{\sqrt{6}}{3}$

C. $\frac{2}{3}$

D. $\frac{4}{9}$

Please reason step by step and put the final answer within \boxed{}.<|im_end|>
